---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'Methodology | hostileworkcalc.com';
const description = 'How the hostile work environment damages calculator works: Title VII caps, severity tiers, and economic damages.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <h1>Methodology</h1>
  <p><em>Reviewed by Riley Chen (RC), Employment &amp; Civil Rights Practice Lead. Updated May 2026.</em></p>
  <h2>Title VII compensatory/punitive caps</h2><p>42 U.S.C. § 1981a caps combined compensatory + punitive damages: $50K (15–100 employees), $100K (101–200), $200K (201–500), $300K (500+). The calculator applies these caps to the non-economic component. Back pay and front pay are equitable remedies not subject to the caps.</p>
  <h2>Severity tiers</h2><p>Severe (single egregious incident): 70% of cap. Pervasive (ongoing pattern): 50% of cap. Moderate (recurring but less extreme): 25% of cap. These reflect published research on Title VII jury verdicts by severity category.</p>
  <h2>Economic damages</h2><p>Back pay: salary/12 × months lost. Front pay: 50% of annual salary for constructive discharge cases. Both added to capped non-economic damages for total estimate.</p>
</BaseLayout>
